# Kyverno policies gating the Meridian slice's rollouts, on kind, stock Sveltos
# v1.15.0 and ConfigHub v0.6.5, 2026-09-28. See docs/user/policy-checks.md.
#
# The checker: Kyverno 3.8.2 on the management cluster in namespace
# policy-checker, holding one ClusterPolicy, disallow-latest-tag (Enforce,
# Pods and, through Kyverno's autogen, Deployments). A local cub worker
# (v0.6.5, built from github.com/confighub/sdk) ran vet-kyverno-server against
# it through a port-forward. The trigger `kyverno` lives in the Space
# mer-policies; the Filter mer-policies/policy-triggers selects it, and every
# Meridian base, class base and variant was given that filter.
#
# 1-5 make a change the policy forbids (the cleanup controller on :latest)
# and show both gates holding it. 6-9 stop the checker's worker and show a
# change going out unchecked. 10 onwards adds a required PolicyCheck and
# rolls a real change out through every stage with approvals and checks.
# Probe change orders were aborted and undone with cub variant demote; the
# fleet ends as it began, plus two owner and cost-centre labels. In the
# owner-label rollout, the recording's own shell loop first passed the four
# prod Spaces as one word ("not found"); that pass was run again, below it.

== warn mode: a change at the root that the policy forbids
